  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133828,
      "id": "16a9183a-68b4-5bad-b2d8-3bcf6597f263",
      "title": "Evaluating Line Integrals of a Vector-Valued Functions Over Plane Curves"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "83829afc-433d-54f3-b068-fd1b2c108308",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(x^{2} y)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,1].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 t,\\quad y=t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(x^{2} y)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(2 t\\right)^{2} \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(\\left(2 t\\right) + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(4 t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(4 t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(1)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(4 t^{3})\\cdot(2)+(2 t + 1)\\cdot(1) \\\\ &=\\left({8 t^{3}}\\right)+\\left({2 t + 1}\\right) \\\\ &=8 t^{3} + 2 t + 1\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({8 t^{3} + 2 t + 1}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{2 t^{4} + t^{2} + t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&((1)+(1)+(2)) \\\\ &{} -((0)+(0)+(0))\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(4)-(0) \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
