    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e0fffaeb-3df8-5934-acab-e2dd56dec891",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(2 y)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 x)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,3].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t,\\quad y=t^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(2 y)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 x)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\left(2 \\left(t^{2}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(2 \\left(t\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2 t^{2})\\cdot(1)+(2 t)\\cdot(2 t) \\\\ &=\\left({2 t^{2}}\\right)+\\left({4 t^{2}}\\right) \\\\ &=6 t^{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{3}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{3}\\left({6 t^{2}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{2 t^{3}}\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ &=((54))-((0)) \\\\ &=(54)-(0) \\\\ &=54\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
